From 000ec23a7ba5dbc8d307ed7a47056382219a5f88 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Glib Shpychka <23005347+gshpychka@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 00:56:17 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] fix(acp): own raw-harness spawns under the requesting agent

Backport of openclaw/openclaw#166908 (4e7a4aa482a) to 2026.10.1. A
sessions_spawn ACP target that is a raw harness id now mints, stores and
dispatches its session under the requesting agent, or the configured ACP
alias, with the harness as the session's runtime. acp.defaultAgent
resolves through the same alias lookup as an explicit agentId. Resume
accepts a record only when its backend and harness match, and also finds
records stored under the harness id.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LNTt5yXBj4uDUwJmPGvXLd
